installation:
## Hosted MCP (recommended)

Add to your OpenCode MCP config:

```json
{
  "mcp": {
    "contextstream": {
      "url": "https://mcp.contextstream.io/mcp"
    }
  }
}
```

Site: https://contextstream.io
OSS server: https://github.com/contextstream/mcp-server

OpenCode 2, in `~/.config/opencode/cli.json`:

```json
{
  "plugins": ["-opencode.sidebar.context", "opencode-cost-details"]
}
```

OpenCode 1, in `~/.config/opencode/tui.json`:

```json
{ "plugin": ["opencode-cost-details"] }
```

Add to your `opencode.json` (or `~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc`):

```json
{
  "plugin": [
    "opencode-craft"
  ]
}
```

Add the package to your OpenCode config:

```json
{
  "plugin": ["@leonardmeagher2/opencode-tasksmd"]
}
```

Install the /call-me iPhone app and open My Number. Then add the remote MCP server to `opencode.json` (or `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json`):
```json
{
  "mcp": {
    "call-me": {
      "type": "remote",
      "url": "https://callmemcp.com/mcp",
      "enabled": true
    }
  }
}
```
Tell the agent your 10-digit /call-me number, or ask it to call the `setup` tool.

Add the server to `opencode.json`, then run `opencode mcp auth employed` to sign in:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "mcp": { "employed": { "type": "remote", "url": "https://jobs.guaqai.me/mcp" } }
}
```

For the job-search skills, copy the repository's `skills/*` into `.agents/skills/`.

Keep Infiknit open, then add a local stdio MCP server:

{
  "mcp": {
    "Infiknit": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": ["node", "plugins/infiknit/bin/infiknit-mcp.cjs"]
    }
  }
}

Clone https://github.com/Synthenova/infiknit-mcp and point the command at that launcher. Do not use a remote 127.0.0.1 URL.

From a reviewed checkout of the source repository, copy
`skills/scvd-general-store` and `skills/scvd-x402-verification` into your
project's `.opencode/skills/` directory, keeping each SKILL.md unchanged.
Merge this remote server into your existing OpenCode configuration:

```json
{
  "mcp": {
    "scvd-general-store": {
      "type": "remote",
      "url": "https://scvd.store/mcp",
      "enabled": true
    }
  }
}
```

Ask OpenCode to load `scvd-x402-verification` and run the free
`preflight_endpoint` for a URL. Inspect the returned verdict, reached level
and missing evidence. An unpaid reading does not prove payment or delivery.

Add the server to `opencode.json` (project) or
`~/.config/opencode/opencode.json` (global):

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "mcp": {
    "springbrand": {
      "type": "remote",
      "url": "https://connector.springbrand.ai/mcp",
      "enabled": true
    }
  }
}
```

No `headers` entry is needed. The server answers unauthenticated requests
with `401` plus a `WWW-Authenticate` challenge, so OpenCode starts its OAuth
flow on first use. To trigger it manually:

```bash
opencode mcp auth springbrand
```

Skill over HTTP (always current, no install):

```json
{ "skills": { "urls": ["https://stacktr.ee/.well-known/skills/"] } }
```

MCP server (adds publish/update tools):

```json
{
  "mcp": {
    "stacktree": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": ["npx", "-y", "stacktree-mcp"],
      "enabled": true,
      "environment": { "STACKTREE_API_KEY": "{env:STACKTREE_API_KEY}" }
    }
  }
}
```

Or run `npx stacktree-install` and pick OpenCode, which writes both.

For OpenCode V2, set BAIZHI_API_KEY in the OpenCode process environment and
add this server to opencode.jsonc. Keep the key out of the config file:

{
  "mcp": {
    "servers": {
      "baizhi": {
        "type": "remote",
        "url": "https://agent-toolkit.app.baizhi.cloud/mcp",
        "oauth": false,
        "headers": {
          "Authorization": "Bearer {env:BAIZHI_API_KEY}"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

Run `opencode mcp list` to check the connection before using any tools.

Add the remote server to `opencode.json`:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "mcp": {
    "outagedeck": {
      "type": "remote",
      "url": "https://outagedeck.com/api/mcp"
    }
  }
}
```

Then ask OpenCode: `Check AWS, GitHub, and Cloudflare for active incidents before changing deployment code. use outagedeck`
